! DFT+U with a stress tensor: the case the Hubbard projectors' strain matters in.
!
! `ni-ldau-nospin.in` with `tstress = .true.` and `verbosity = 'high'`. The
! Hubbard energy depends on the cell exactly the way it depends on the atomic
! positions -- through projectors that are atomic orbitals at `k + G` -- so the
! stress reaches it by differentiating through them, which is the whole of QE's
! `stres_hub.f90` (2291 lines) obtained without transcribing any of it.
!
! It is also the case that catches the k-point trap of this phase: `KPoints.coords`
! are in units of a *static* alat, so under a strain the k-points have to be
! carried to the new reciprocal cell by hand, and a Hubbard projector built at
! the old ones is wrong without being an error. QE prints a `hubbard stress`
! row at this verbosity, so the term is compared on its own.
 &control
    calculation='scf'
    tstress = .true.
    verbosity = 'high'
 /
 &system
    ibrav=2, celldm(1) =6.48, nat=1, ntyp=1,
    nspin=1,
    ecutwfc = 24.0, ecutrho = 288.0,
    occupations='smearing', smearing='marzari-vanderbilt', degauss=0.02
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr=1.0e-10
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Ni 58.69 Ni.pz-nd-rrkjus.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS {alat}
 Ni 0.0 0.0 0.0
K_POINTS {automatic}
 4 4 4 1 1 1
HUBBARD {atomic}
U Ni-3d 3.0
